---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;padding:56px 26px 40px">
    <div style="font:600 11px/1 var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:16px">About</div>
    <h1 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:38px;letter-spacing:-.015em;color:var(--ink);margin:0 0 24px">Q's Notes</h1>

    <div class="prose-body">
      <p>Hi, I'm Q.</p>
      <p>
        This is a personal, bilingual notebook — notes, essays, and opinions on AI, agents,
        software, business, and consulting, with the occasional aside on games, books, films, or
        culture. It's tended, not published: pieces arrive early as <em>seedlings</em>, get argued
        and sourced into <em>growing</em> notes, and settle into <em>evergreen</em> ones only when I
        stand behind them as written.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every piece has an English and a Chinese version — transcreations, not literal translations,
        so each reads like it was written in its own language. Most come out of a small weekly
        writing loop rather than ad-hoc posting; the point of view is the only part that stays
        manual.
      </p>
      <p>That's pretty much it. Look around, or subscribe by <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
